<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5379" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭpĕdālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>two feet long</i>, <i>broad</i>, or <i>thick</i> (class. in prose and poetry): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fenestrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 14, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trabes,</span>”
				<i>two feet thick</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 4, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">materia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. B.
					C. 2, 10</span></i>
			: sol huic (Epicuro) bipedalis fortasse videtur, *
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fin. 1, 6, 20</span></i>: adulescentulus bipedali minor, *
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 43</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tegulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
					1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modulus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 3, 309</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hiatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 12, 23, § 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latitudo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 3, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭpĕdāle</span></b> ,
			is, n., <i>a tile</i> or <i>flag-stone two feet long</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Fabr. p. 500, 39</span></i>.</div>
